    "result_text": "All 256 tests pass, including the two new `AcceptanceTest` segment tests. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner response.\n\n**What the spec required:** return `ownerSegment` formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>` \u2014 TIER = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel \u2265 3` else `STANDARD`; AREA = `METRO` when the locality is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD) else `REGIONAL`.\n\n**Changes (two files):**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the Owner response schema (after `timezone`). The `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this spec, so this creates the field/getter/setter the mapper targets.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", expression = \"java(ownerSegment(owner))\")` plus an `ownerSegment(owner)` default method that composes the two existing derived values: `membershipLevel(owner)` for TIER and `locality(owner)` for AREA (a locality is \"known\" iff `PostcodeRegions.timezoneForRegion` returns non-null, i.e. NSW/VIC/QLD), keeping it consistent with the existing locality/timezone logic.\n\nThe new tests confirm a new owner with an email (membershipLevel 2 \u2192 STANDARD) yields `STANDARD_METRO` in Sydney (NSW) and `STANDARD_REGIONAL` in an unknown city. Full suite: **256 passed, 0 failures**.",
